    "$comment-terms": "Below this line the licence is a published set of terms rather than a text anybody may redistribute, so the screen links to it instead of carrying it. A 'file' is what separates the two. A licence with \"notices\": true is the third case: an aggregate notices document that the licences inside a native library require to travel with it, so it ships, and that is far too long to read in a dialog, so the screen links to the copy on rpmrpmrpm.com. It needs both a file and a url.",
